
Note :- 
Important file checking operators in bash script if writing ?

    Operator	Meaning
        -f	Checks regular file exists
        -d	Checks directory exists
        -e	Checks whether file or directory exists
        -r	Checks read permission
        -w	Checks write permission
        -x	Checks execute permission
        -s	Checks file exists and is not empty

ii)
Left side of assignment → No $.

eg :- for (( $num1=0; $num1<11; $num1++ ))  //wrong
      for (( num1=0; num1<11; num1++ ))   //right 
     

